{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/463010-six-of-vii-blood-and-smoke-and-the-betrayed","id":463010,"title":"Six of VII: Blood and Smoke and the Betrayed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-30T19:44:45-07:00","id":463010,"title":"Six of VII: Blood and Smoke and the Betrayed","content":"I've always loved the <b>VII </b>sourcebook. VII is an antagonist you can hang a lot of hats on, and that book represents a lot of the fun one can have with the tool box aesthetic. In particular, I'm a big fan of the Akhud; they're my favourite version of VII. However, the Akhud have seen a lot of homebrew second edition action. There are quite a few Praestantias floating around, for instance.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I thought I'd have a look at one of the stranger versions of VII: <b>The Betrayed</b>.<br /> <br /> In this version of VII (<b>spoilers?</b>), the Covenant is made up of six bloodlines of vampires who claim descent from a ghouled King of Russia/Ukraine. In short, the king was betrayed when his master, one of the Kindred, murdered seven members of his royal house. In rage, the king ate the vampire's heart, and was damned himself. The souls of the seven slain family members haunt his descendents to this day, urging them to exact their vengeance on the Kindred. This history is briefly mentioned in the write-up for VII in <b>Vampire: The Requiem, Second Edition</b>.<br /> <br /> The Betrayed are made up of seven Houses. The Houses are a cross between Clans and Covenants: one can be Embraced into a House, but join another House and gain the equivalent of their Covenant advantage. Originally, there were seven houses, but one fell (I can't recall why at the moment).<br /> <br /> For now, I've just converted weaknesses to banes, and made the House advantages more uniform. There are a lot more moving parts to play around with. That, and the ink hasn't really dried on these yet, and I'm already questioning some of my choices. Your feedback is valued, as always.<br /> <br /> Anyway, without further ado:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35eVUwSWdUSjF4TUU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35eVUwSWdUSjF4TUU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35eVUwSWdUSjF4TUU/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35eVUwSWdUSjF4TUU/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (To understand this document, and what the heck I'm talking about in general, you'll probably need to have access to the <b>VII </b>book.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More